Canonical directory view for text-to-SQL. Query ONLY this view (FROM orgs_llm).
Audience columns (works_with_*): a non-empty value is usually Directly or Indirectly.
Filter those with: col IS NOT NULL AND TRIM(col) != '' (do not require the word Yes).

View name: orgs_llm
Columns:
  - org_name (TEXT) [populated 101/101] examples: "PECT", "Kestrix", "AXIS CLC"
  - department_or_unit (TEXT) [populated 25/101] examples: "Housing", "NookCRM", "BrumEnergy"
  - org_main_type (TEXT) [populated 101/101] examples: "Consultant or advisor", "Product manufacturer / supplier", "Academic department / group / network"
  - org_type_other_public (TEXT) [populated 3/101] examples: "General Further Education College", "Joint Industry/Government sector council", "A new organisation formed by a combination of local and combined authorities"
  - org_type_other_private (TEXT) [populated 11/101] examples: "Magazine", "Data company", "Consumer Code"
  - org_type_other_nonprofit (TEXT) [populated 19/101] examples: "Charity", "consultant", "Retrofit Hub"
  - county (TEXT) [populated 101/101] examples: "Kent (England)", "Cardiff (Wales)", "Devon (England)"
  - postcode (TEXT) [populated 99/101] examples: "B1 2AJ", "G2 3EX", "G4 9RH"
  - local_authority (TEXT) [populated 98/101] examples: "Arun", "York", "Derby"
  - parish (TEXT) [populated 96/101] examples: "Frome", "Lewes", "Euxton"
  - hq_latitude (REAL) [populated 98/101] examples: "52.3963", "51.36486", "51.38666"
